 ## Background
-This method is described in the context of the Tsplat project, which aims to run Gaussian splatting in a terminal environment [S1, unofficial]. It is part of the broader effort to optimize 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization, as surveyed in recent literature [S2, unofficial]. The use of radix sort for depth sorting in splatting is a common optimization to replace slower comparison-based sorts.
+This method is described in the context of optimizing 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization pipelines [S1, unofficial]. It is part of the broader effort to accelerate splatting by replacing slower comparison-based sorts with hardware-friendly radix sorts [S2, unofficial]. The use of a 2-pass 16-bit radix sort on float bit patterns is a standard optimization for depth sorting in GPU rendering [G].
 
